                <pb facs="0521" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3365: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-04T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 4—11:40
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>126. With financial aid of Japanese, Tuan Ch’i-jui and Hsu Shucheng are forming
                    military force to take aggressive action against supporters of Canton
                    government. The President may give up office. He feels disheartened. As yet
                    formation of cabinet is not completed. Condition of country is serious.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
